{"id":"p10-l06","minutes":35,"summary":"Register code lives on masks and shifts, and one wrong parenthesis or a signed 1 &lt;&lt; 31 corrupts a neighbouring field. You derive field insert and extract, write SET_BIT, CLEAR_BIT and field macros with host tests over every position and width, then compile a polling loop for a Cortex-M3 and read the assembly to see exactly what volatile changes.","html":"<h2 id=\"masks-and-shifts\">Masks and shifts</h2>\n<p>A register field is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span> bits starting at bit <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span></span></span></span>. Everything follows from one mask:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7977em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7144em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.109em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6891em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≪</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>extract</strong>: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">get</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≫</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">&amp;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li>\n<li><strong>insert</strong>: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">←</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">&amp;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∼</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.109em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">((</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">&amp;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≪</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></li>\n<li><strong>set / clear / toggle bit <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span></strong>: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6835em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≪</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">&amp;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.3669em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∼</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≪</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.25em;\"><span class=\"mord\">^</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6835em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≪</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Three bugs show up in nearly every codebase:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Signed shifts.</strong> <code>1 &lt;&lt; 31</code> shifts a signed <code>int</code> into its sign bit, which is undefined behaviour in C. Always use <code>1u</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Width 32.</strong> <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">32</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> via <code>(1u &lt;&lt; 32) - 1</code> is also undefined (shift ≥ width). Use <code>0xFFFFFFFFu &gt;&gt; (32 - w)</code>, valid for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7804em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7719em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">32</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li><strong>Unmasked values.</strong> Inserting <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span></span></span></span> without <code>&amp; m_w</code> lets an oversized value spill into the next field.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Macros must parenthesise every argument, so <code>FIELD_GET(x | y, 4, 2)</code> doesn’t parse as <code>x | (y &gt;&gt; 4)</code>.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"regview\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>A 32-bit register, bit by bit. Pick a position and width, and a value to insert. The mask, the cleared register and the result are shown in binary; an unmasked insert shows the spill into the neighbouring field.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"what-volatile-means\">What volatile means</h2>\n<p><code>volatile</code> tells the compiler that every read and write of the object is an observable side effect: it must perform each access, in program order, and it can’t keep the value in a register or assume it hasn’t changed. A hardware status register changes on its own, so code that polls it <strong>must</strong> read through a <code>volatile</code> lvalue:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-c\">while (!(USART1-&gt;SR &amp; USART_SR_TXE)) {}   /* SR is declared volatile uint32_t */\n</code></pre>\n<p>Without <code>volatile</code>, the optimiser sees a loop that never writes the variable, concludes the condition can’t change, loads it once and spins forever. You’ll see this in the assembly below.</p>\n<p>What volatile does <strong>not</strong> do: it doesn’t make a read-modify-write atomic, it doesn’t order accesses to non-volatile variables, and it doesn’t add memory barriers between cores or DMA. For sharing data with interrupts you still need the techniques in lesson 10.</p>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>Insert the value 5 into a 3-bit field at bit 4 of a register holding 0xFFFF_FF0F.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">7</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6835em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">7</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≪</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mord\">70</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Clear: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">&amp;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∼</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mord\">70</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span></span></span></span> (those bits were already zero).</li>\n<li>Insert: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">&amp;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">7</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≪</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mord\">50</span></span></span></span>, giving <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Extract back: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≫</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">&amp;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">7</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Unmasked insert of 13: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6835em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">13</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≪</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span> sets bit 7, which belongs to the next field.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n<p>The top of <code>bits_test.c</code> is the macro header (what you would put in <code>bits.h</code>), and the rest tests every position and width against a bit-by-bit reference. <code>poll.c</code> is two polling loops for the Cortex-M3, and <code>check_volatile.py</code> compiles them with <code>-O2</code> and reads the assembly.</p>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">bits_test.c</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;stdint.h&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;stdlib.h&gt;</span></span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* ---- bits.h ---- */</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> BIT(n)                 (1u &lt;&lt; (n))</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> SET_BIT(r, n)          ((r) |= BIT(n))</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> CLEAR_BIT(r, n)        ((r) &amp;= ~BIT(n))</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> TOGGLE_BIT(r, n)       ((r) ^= BIT(n))</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> READ_BIT(r, n)         (((r) &gt;&gt; (n)) &amp; 1u)</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> FIELD_MASK_W(w)        (0xFFFFFFFFu &gt;&gt; (32u - (w)))            <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* valid for 1 &lt;= w &lt;= 32 */</span></span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> FIELD_MASK(p, w)       (FIELD_MASK_W(w) &lt;&lt; (p))</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> FIELD_GET(r, p, w)     (((r) &gt;&gt; (p)) &amp; FIELD_MASK_W(w))</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> FIELD_PREP(p, w, v)    ((((uint32_t)(v)) &amp; FIELD_MASK_W(w)) &lt;&lt; (p))</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> FIELD_SET(r, p, w, v)  ((r) = ((r) &amp; ~FIELD_MASK(p, w)) | FIELD_PREP(p, w, v))</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* ---------------- */</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> rng = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0x12345678u</span>;\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">next</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">void</span>)</span> { rng ^= rng &lt;&lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">13</span>; rng ^= rng &gt;&gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">17</span>; rng ^= rng &lt;&lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> rng; }\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* slow, obviously-correct reference: one bit at a time */</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">ref_set</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> r, <span class=\"hljs-type\">unsigned</span> p, <span class=\"hljs-type\">unsigned</span> w, <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> v)</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">unsigned</span> i = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; i &lt; w; i++) { <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> b = (v &gt;&gt; i) &amp; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1u</span>; r = (r &amp; ~(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1u</span> &lt;&lt; (p + i))) | (b &lt;&lt; (p + i)); }\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> r;\n}\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> CHECK(c) do { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (!(c)) { printf(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;FAIL line %d (p=%u w=%u)\\n&quot;</span>, __LINE__, p, w); exit(1); } } while (0)</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">main</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">void</span>)</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">unsigned</span> cases = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, p = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, w = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>;\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (p = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; p &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">32</span>; p++)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (w = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>; w &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">32</span> - p; w++)\n      <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> k = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; k &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>; k++) {\n        <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> r = next(), v = next(), r0 = r;\n        FIELD_SET(r, p, w, v);\n        CHECK(r == ref_set(r0, p, w, v));                          <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* matches the reference */</span>\n        CHECK(FIELD_GET(r, p, w) == (v &amp; FIELD_MASK_W(w)));        <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* reads back */</span>\n        CHECK((r &amp; ~FIELD_MASK(p, w)) == (r0 &amp; ~FIELD_MASK(p, w))); <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* neighbours untouched */</span>\n        cases++;\n      }\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (p = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; p &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">32</span>; p++) {\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> r = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; SET_BIT(r, p); CHECK(r == (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1u</span> &lt;&lt; p) &amp;&amp; READ_BIT(r, p) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>);\n    TOGGLE_BIT(r, p); CHECK(r == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>); r = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0xFFFFFFFFu</span>; CLEAR_BIT(r, p); CHECK(r == ~(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1u</span> &lt;&lt; p));\n  }\n  p = <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>; w = <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>;\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> r = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0xFFFFFF0Fu</span>; FIELD_SET(r, <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>); CHECK(r == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0xFFFFFF5Fu</span> &amp;&amp; FIELD_GET(r, <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>);\n  CHECK(FIELD_MASK_W(<span class=\"hljs-number\">32</span>) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0xFFFFFFFFu</span> &amp;&amp; FIELD_MASK(<span class=\"hljs-number\">31</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0x80000000u</span>);\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> a = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0x0F</span>, b = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0x30</span>; CHECK(FIELD_GET(a | b, <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>);   <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* argument parenthesised */</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">printf</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;%u field cases and 32 single-bit cases passed\\nPASS\\n&quot;</span>, cases);\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>;\n}</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"1\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">poll.c</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"1\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"1\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;stdint.h&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> status_plain;              <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* imagine an ISR or the hardware sets bit 0 */</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">volatile</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> status_vol;\n\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">void</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">wait_plain</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">void</span>)</span>    { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">while</span> (!(status_plain &amp; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1u</span>)) {} }\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">void</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">wait_volatile</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">void</span>)</span> { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">while</span> (!(status_vol &amp; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1u</span>)) {} }</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"2\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">check_volatile.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"2\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"2\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Compile poll.c with -O2 for a Cortex-M3 and check where the loads are.&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> re, shutil, subprocess, sys\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> shutil.which(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;arm-none-eabi-gcc&quot;</span>):\n    sys.exit(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;needs arm-none-eabi-gcc (Debian/Ubuntu: apt install gcc-arm-none-eabi)&quot;</span>)\nasm = subprocess.run([<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;arm-none-eabi-gcc&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;-mcpu=cortex-m3&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;-mthumb&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;-O2&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;-S&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;poll.c&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;-o&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;-&quot;</span>],\n                     capture_output=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">True</span>, text=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">True</span>, check=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">True</span>).stdout\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">body</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">name</span>):\n    lines = asm.split(name + <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;:\\n&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>].split(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;\\t.size&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>].splitlines()\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> [l.strip() <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> l <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> lines <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> l.strip() <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> l.strip().startswith((<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;@&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;.&quot;</span>))\n            <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">or</span> re.<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">match</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">r&quot;^\\.L\\d+:&quot;</span>, l.strip())]\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">loop</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">lines</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Instructions between a label and the branch that jumps back to it.&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> i, l <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">enumerate</span>(lines):\n        m = re.<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">match</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">r&quot;^(\\.L\\d+):$&quot;</span>, l)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> m:\n            <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> j <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(i + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(lines)):\n                <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> lines[j].endswith(m.group(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> lines[j].split()[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>].startswith(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;b&quot;</span>):\n                    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> lines[i + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>:j + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> []\n\nplain, vol = loop(body(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;wait_plain&quot;</span>)), loop(body(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;wait_volatile&quot;</span>))\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;plain loop:   &quot;</span>, plain)\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;volatile loop:&quot;</span>, vol)\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> plain <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">any</span>(l.startswith(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;ldr&quot;</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> l <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> plain)    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># loaded once, then spins forever</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">any</span>(l.startswith(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;ldr&quot;</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> l <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> vol)                     <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># re-reads memory every iteration</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why is <code>#define FIELD_GET(r, p, w) r &gt;&gt; p &amp; FIELD_MASK_W(w)</code> wrong even though it often works?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Without parentheses, <code>FIELD_GET(x | y, 4, 2)</code> expands to <code>x | y &gt;&gt; 4 &amp; 3</code>, which C parses as <code>x | ((y &gt;&gt; 4) &amp; 3)</code>, because <code>&gt;&gt;</code> and <code>&amp;</code> bind tighter than <code>|</code>. Every macro argument, and the whole expansion, needs parentheses.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>A flag <code>done</code> is set in an ISR and polled in <code>main</code>. You add <code>volatile</code> and it works. A colleague says volatile makes it thread-safe. Is that right?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Only for this case: a single aligned 32-bit store by the ISR and loads by main are each atomic on Cortex-M, and volatile forces main to re-read. But <code>count++</code> on a volatile is still load, add, store, and an interrupt between them loses an update. Volatile gives visibility, not atomicity (lesson 10).</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p10-l06\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"masks-and-shifts","title":"Masks and shifts"},{"id":"what-volatile-means","title":"What volatile means"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p10-l06-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Mask (decimal) of a 3-bit field at bit 4?</p>\n","explain":"<p>0x70.</p>\n","answer":112,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p10-l06-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Result (decimal) of inserting 5 into that field of 0xFFFFFF0F?</p>\n","explain":"<p>0xFFFFFF5F.</p>\n","answer":4294967135,"tol":1e-7,"unit":""},{"id":"p10-l06-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Extract the 4-bit field at bit 8 of 0x00003A00 (decimal)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>0xA.</p>\n","answer":10,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p10-l06-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>How many (position, width) pairs are there for fields inside a 32-bit register?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The test loops over all 528.</p>\n","answer":528,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p10-l06-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>What is wrong with 1 &lt;&lt; 31 in C?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Use 1u &lt;&lt; 31.</p>\n","options":["nothing","it shifts a signed int into the sign bit, which is undefined behaviour","it is too slow","it equals zero"],"answer":1},{"id":"p10-l06-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>What does volatile guarantee?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Visibility, not atomicity.</p>\n","options":["atomic read-modify-write","every access is performed, in order, and not cached in a register","mutual exclusion with interrupts","memory barriers for DMA"],"answer":1}],"code":[{"file":"bits_test.c","lang":"c","src":"#include <stdint.h>\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\n/* ---- bits.h ---- */\n#define BIT(n)                 (1u << (n))\n#define SET_BIT(r, n)          ((r) |= BIT(n))\n#define CLEAR_BIT(r, n)        ((r) &= ~BIT(n))\n#define TOGGLE_BIT(r, n)       ((r) ^= BIT(n))\n#define READ_BIT(r, n)         (((r) >> (n)) & 1u)\n#define FIELD_MASK_W(w)        (0xFFFFFFFFu >> (32u - (w)))            /* valid for 1 <= w <= 32 */\n#define FIELD_MASK(p, w)       (FIELD_MASK_W(w) << (p))\n#define FIELD_GET(r, p, w)     (((r) >> (p)) & FIELD_MASK_W(w))\n#define FIELD_PREP(p, w, v)    ((((uint32_t)(v)) & FIELD_MASK_W(w)) << (p))\n#define FIELD_SET(r, p, w, v)  ((r) = ((r) & ~FIELD_MASK(p, w)) | FIELD_PREP(p, w, v))\n/* ---------------- */\n\nstatic uint32_t rng = 0x12345678u;\nstatic uint32_t next(void) { rng ^= rng << 13; rng ^= rng >> 17; rng ^= rng << 5; return rng; }\n\n/* slow, obviously-correct reference: one bit at a time */\nstatic uint32_t ref_set(uint32_t r, unsigned p, unsigned w, uint32_t v) {\n  for (unsigned i = 0; i < w; i++) { uint32_t b = (v >> i) & 1u; r = (r & ~(1u << (p + i))) | (b << (p + i)); }\n  return r;\n}\n#define CHECK(c) do { if (!(c)) { printf(\"FAIL line %d (p=%u w=%u)\\n\", __LINE__, p, w); exit(1); } } while (0)\n\nint main(void) {\n  unsigned cases = 0, p = 0, w = 0;\n  for (p = 0; p < 32; p++)\n    for (w = 1; w <= 32 - p; w++)\n      for (int k = 0; k < 50; k++) {\n        uint32_t r = next(), v = next(), r0 = r;\n        FIELD_SET(r, p, w, v);\n        CHECK(r == ref_set(r0, p, w, v));                          /* matches the reference */\n        CHECK(FIELD_GET(r, p, w) == (v & FIELD_MASK_W(w)));        /* reads back */\n        CHECK((r & ~FIELD_MASK(p, w)) == (r0 & ~FIELD_MASK(p, w))); /* neighbours untouched */\n        cases++;\n      }\n  for (p = 0; p < 32; p++) {\n    uint32_t r = 0; SET_BIT(r, p); CHECK(r == (1u << p) && READ_BIT(r, p) == 1);\n    TOGGLE_BIT(r, p); CHECK(r == 0); r = 0xFFFFFFFFu; CLEAR_BIT(r, p); CHECK(r == ~(1u << p));\n  }\n  p = 4; w = 3;\n  uint32_t r = 0xFFFFFF0Fu; FIELD_SET(r, 4, 3, 5); CHECK(r == 0xFFFFFF5Fu && FIELD_GET(r, 4, 3) == 5);\n  CHECK(FIELD_MASK_W(32) == 0xFFFFFFFFu && FIELD_MASK(31, 1) == 0x80000000u);\n  uint32_t a = 0x0F, b = 0x30; CHECK(FIELD_GET(a | b, 4, 2) == 3);   /* argument parenthesised */\n  printf(\"%u field cases and 32 single-bit cases passed\\nPASS\\n\", cases);\n  return 0;\n}"},{"file":"poll.c","lang":"c","src":"#include <stdint.h>\nuint32_t status_plain;              /* imagine an ISR or the hardware sets bit 0 */\nvolatile uint32_t status_vol;\n\nvoid wait_plain(void)    { while (!(status_plain & 1u)) {} }\nvoid wait_volatile(void) { while (!(status_vol & 1u)) {} }"},{"file":"check_volatile.py","lang":"python","src":"\"\"\"Compile poll.c with -O2 for a Cortex-M3 and check where the loads are.\"\"\"\nimport re, shutil, subprocess, sys\nif not shutil.which(\"arm-none-eabi-gcc\"):\n    sys.exit(\"needs arm-none-eabi-gcc (Debian/Ubuntu: apt install gcc-arm-none-eabi)\")\nasm = subprocess.run([\"arm-none-eabi-gcc\", \"-mcpu=cortex-m3\", \"-mthumb\", \"-O2\", \"-S\", \"poll.c\", \"-o\", \"-\"],\n                     capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout\n\ndef body(name):\n    lines = asm.split(name + \":\\n\", 1)[1].split(\"\\t.size\", 1)[0].splitlines()\n    return [l.strip() for l in lines if l.strip() and not l.strip().startswith((\"@\", \".\"))\n            or re.match(r\"^\\.L\\d+:\", l.strip())]\n\ndef loop(lines):\n    \"\"\"Instructions between a label and the branch that jumps back to it.\"\"\"\n    for i, l in enumerate(lines):\n        m = re.match(r\"^(\\.L\\d+):$\", l)\n        if m:\n            for j in range(i + 1, len(lines)):\n                if lines[j].endswith(m.group(1)) and lines[j].split()[0].startswith(\"b\"):\n                    return lines[i + 1:j + 1]\n    return []\n\nplain, vol = loop(body(\"wait_plain\")), loop(body(\"wait_volatile\"))\nprint(\"plain loop:   \", plain)\nprint(\"volatile loop:\", vol)\nassert plain and not any(l.startswith(\"ldr\") for l in plain)    # loaded once, then spins forever\nassert any(l.startswith(\"ldr\") for l in vol)                     # re-reads memory every iteration\nprint(\"PASS\")"}]}